---
term: Constituent corporation
aka:
  - Subordinate corporation
section: structure
order: 40
definition: A corporation that belongs to a [[parent corporation]] and takes part in the parent's governance.
seeAlso:
  - sibling-corporation
  - nested-corporation
---
Constituents keep substantial autonomy. They accept the parent's authority only on matters within the parent's [[higher-order common interest]], such as conflicts with siblings or effects that spill beyond their own jurisdiction.
